# CODEOWNERS — review routing for the Forge hub (capability hub-contribution-policy).
#
# Current state: the askenaz-dev org has no GitHub teams yet, and the EMU CLI
# auth cannot create them (org-level write). Until an org owner provisions the
# teams via the GitHub web UI, the maintainer is the catch-all owner so every
# contribution PR still requires a CODEOWNERS review (gate 1).
#
# Target state: route each component to the GitHub team mapped from its
# owner_team. Uncomment the per-team block below once the teams exist, and
# add a line per new component (its owner_team → team). See CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# Bot exclusion (capability portal-gitops-write, decision D3): the web-PR
# contribution path is mediated by a portal-owned GitHub App ("the bot") that
# opens PRs but cannot merge. The bot's identity MUST NOT appear as an owner in
# this file, on ANY line. Branch protection requires a CODEOWNERS approval from
# a reviewer who is NOT the PR author; since the bot authors web-path PRs, an
# owner here is always a non-bot human/team — so the bot can never satisfy its
# own required review. Keep it that way: never add the App / its bot account as
# a code owner. A leaked bot token can therefore open PRs but never land one.

# --- catch-all (transitional, NON-bot owner) ---
*                                   @askenaz

# --- target per-component routing (uncomment once teams are provisioned) ---
# skills/design-system/             @askenaz-dev/design-platform
# rules/no-console-log/             @askenaz-dev/dx-platform
# agents/forge-pr-writer/           @askenaz-dev/dx-platform
# hooks/doctor-on-session-start/    @askenaz-dev/dx-platform
#
# The catalog + registry are admin-owned:
# hub/                              @askenaz-dev/hub-maintainers
# .github/                          @askenaz-dev/hub-maintainers
# tools/                            @askenaz-dev/hub-maintainers
